---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Your First 50 Subscribers in 7 Days — The Guide | Redefining Retirement"
  description="The full 3-step playbook for setting up your system and moving your audience onto your own list, plus the monetization menu for what comes after."
  type="article"
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">

      <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="tag">Free Guide</span>
        <h1 class="article-title">Your First 50 Subscribers in 7 Days</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">
          3 simple steps to set up your system and start moving your audience onto a list you actually own.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ── HELLO ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="hello-section">
        <img
          src="/images/corey-portrait.jpg"
          alt="Corey Koehler"
          class="hello-photo"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
        <div class="hello-text">
          <h2>Hello</h2>
          <p>Hey, I'm Corey Koehler (KOH-ler).</p>
          <p>Foundry worker, then mechanical draftsman for 17 years, then... whatever this is now.</p>
          <p>Back in 2007 I had a fantasy football blog pulling 10,000+ visitors a week from Google. I never collected a single email. Every week I was just hoping Google would send those people back to me — no guarantee, no second chance if it didn't. Eventually it didn't, and I had nothing to show for it.</p>
          <p>A few years later I built another newsletter, this time with the email list as the foundation from day one. That one's still paying off today.</p>
          <p>This guide is the exact playbook I'd use if I were starting from zero today. No 10,000-follower fantasy — just the steps to set up your system and start moving people onto your list this week.</p>
          <p>Let's get into it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── READER TESTIMONIAL ───────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="reader-quote">
        <p>"When I was just getting started with my email newsletter, I didn't have much experience or confidence. Corey walked me through the early steps, gave me clear advice, and helped me find my footing. He made the whole process feel simple and doable.</p>
        <p>Thanks to his coaching, I now have a newsletter that basically runs on autopilot, and it's working great!"</p>
        <p class="reader-quote-attr">— Dustin Hauer, founder of Social Media Bites</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── INTRO VIDEO WALKTHROUGH ──────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="video-block">
        <h3 class="video-block-title">Video walkthrough</h3>
        <p class="video-block-deck">Before we get into setting up your newsletter, watch this short walkthrough of the first two steps.</p>
        <p class="video-block-note">Heads up: Beehiiv has updated its dashboard since I recorded this, so a few screens may look slightly different. The steps and principles are still exactly the same — just follow along for the "why," and use the written steps below for the current click-by-click.</p>
        <div class="video-embed">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.loom.com/embed/c763792cb89348d58cafbd5a9d119249"
            frameborder="0"
            webkitallowfullscreen
            mozallowfullscreen
            allowfullscreen
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── THE HOOK ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="hook-block">
        <h2>Why newsletters crush social for long-term value</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Most creators think their subscriber count equals security. Reality check:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>👉 1,000 social media followers = about $79/month</li>
            <li>👉 1,000 YouTube subs = about $79/month</li>
            <li>👉 1,000 email subs = about $582/month</li>
          </ul>
          <p>That's not my opinion — that's from a Neil Patel study of 2,501 marketers, which found email subscribers generate 7.4x more revenue per month than YouTube subscribers.</p>
          <p>And the kicker? Email subscribers don't vanish when the algorithm decides to ghost you.</p>
          <p>Email subscribers = assets you own. Average lifetime value: $37.85 each (up to $100+ in high-value niches).</p>
          <p>YouTube subs = rented attention. They only pay if they keep watching, and you're at the mercy of RPMs, ad buyers, and YouTube's mood swings.</p>
          <p>A social media follower = more rented attention. Even worse than YouTube in some cases — followers are worth just pennies ($0.01–$0.10).</p>
          <p>Translation: 10,000 social followers might bring in a couple grand if you're lucky.</p>
          <p>10,000 email subs? That could mean a more reliable five-figure monthly income.</p>
          <p>That's the gap. And it's why smart creators are finally saying:</p>
          <p><em>"I'll use YouTube and social for discovery, but my email list is my long-term plan."</em></p>
          <p>Ok, with that out of the way, let's get started on your newsletter…</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── STEPS ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="steps">

        <!-- STEP 1 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 1</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Pick something worth trading an email for</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>A "gift" is just something useful enough that a stranger hands over their email address for it. It doesn't need to be complicated, and it definitely doesn't need to take you a week to make.</p>
              <p>When I did this, I started with stuff I'd already made — a post that did well, an answer to the question people kept asking me. The work was already done. I just packaged it up.</p>
              <p>Don't overthink it. Pick from:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>A "how-to" post or video that already performed well</li>
                <li>An answer to the question you get asked all the time</li>
                <li>Or just open a waitlist and figure out the gift later — that's allowed</li>
              </ul>
              <p>If you're starting from nothing, here's a shortlist of fast ideas:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Checklist</li>
                <li>Quick guide or cheat sheet</li>
                <li>A list of tools, sites, or books you actually use</li>
                <li>A short case study or mini workbook</li>
                <li>Something exclusive — a video, article, or podcast episode</li>
                <li>A mini course or quiz</li>
                <li>A template</li>
              </ul>
              <p>You don't need to build the gift today. Just decide what it is — you'll need it for step 2.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 2 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 2</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Set up your home base</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>I use Beehiiv, and it's what I'd pick again if I were starting today — solid analytics, a built-in referral system, and they don't take a cut of your paid subscriptions.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="inline-cta">
              <p>If you sign up through my link and use the code <strong class="coupon">MIGRATE</strong>, you get 20% off your first three months.</p>
              <a
                href="https://www.beehiiv.com?via=MIGRATE"
                class="btn"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Start on Beehiiv &rarr;
              </a>
              <p class="cta-note">Free plan available. Affiliate link — I earn a small commission at no cost to you.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="prose">
              <p>Think of this as installing the plumbing. Follow it in order — don't skip steps.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Step 1: Pick your platform</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p><strong>Action:</strong> Sign up for Beehiiv.</p>
              <p><strong>Why:</strong> It's simple, powerful, and the one I use myself — plus they don't take a cut of your paid subscriptions.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Step 2: Fill in the basics</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>Go to Settings &rarr; General Info and fill in your details. This part's just data entry.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Step 3: Name your newsletter</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>The rule: clear beats clever, every time.</p>
              <p><strong>Avoid:</strong> something vague like "Marketing Musings."</p>
              <p><strong>Try:</strong> something that tells people exactly what's inside — "[Outcome] for [Audience]."</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Step 4: Write your two-line pitch</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>This is the bit people skip, and shouldn't:</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Line 1 (the hook):</strong> Who it's for + the problem + the outcome</li>
                <li><strong>Line 2 (the lever):</strong> A call to action + the benefit</li>
              </ul>
              <p><em>Example: "Helping parents exhausted by screen-time battles set boundaries that actually stick. Enter your email and join the waitlist to get 5 quick scripts that make unplugging easier."</em></p>
            </div>

            <div class="prompt-block">
              <p class="prompt-label">If you want help writing yours, copy this into ChatGPT (or whatever AI tool you've got open):</p>
              <pre>You are a newsletter growth expert. I want you to help me create a 2-line waitlist pitch for my newsletter.

Walk me through it step by step.

Step 1: Ask me what I want my readers to do (not "learn") and help me phrase it in action terms.

Step 2: Ask me to niche it down. Help me pick a slice of my audience.

Step 3: Ask me to pick 1 problem my audience has and 1 outcome they want. Combine into a single clear sentence.

Step 4: Help me add a call-to-action line that starts with "Enter your email and join the waitlist to get…" and ends with a concrete benefit.

Give me 3 variations of my 2-line waitlist pitch in plain, conversational language.</pre>
            </div>

            <div class="prose">
              <p>A few other basics while you're in there: add a logo and thumbnail (Canva works fine if you don't have one), pick 3 publication tags, and set your language and time zone. Leave everything else for later — we're keeping this simple.</p>
              <p>That's it. Your home base is ready. Next, we'll start inviting people.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEP 3 -->
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">Step 3</div>
          <div class="step-content">
            <h2 class="step-title">Go get your first 50</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>This is the part most people skip past, and it's the part that actually matters. Your goal this week: 50 people. Here's how I'd go after it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="video-embed">
              <iframe
                src="https://www.loom.com/embed/7c909354370d435b91b0019f7cf815fe"
                frameborder="0"
                webkitallowfullscreen
                mozallowfullscreen
                allowfullscreen
              ></iframe>
            </div>

            <div class="prose">
              <h3>1. Reach out directly</h3>
              <p>Message people you actually know. Not a mass blast — a real message, one at a time.</p>
              <blockquote>
                <p><strong>Subject:</strong> Quick question, [First Name]</p>
                <p>Hey [First Name],</p>
                <p>I'm starting a newsletter about [TOPIC], and I'd love to include you.</p>
                <p>Want in? Just reply and let me know.</p>
              </blockquote>
              <p>When they say yes:</p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>Awesome! Just click this link to sign up: [link]</p>
                <p>Or drop me your best email, and I'll add you myself.</p>
              </blockquote>
              <p>After they sign up:</p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>Thank you! By the way, do you know one other person who'd be interested too?</p>
              </blockquote>

              <h3>DM your social connections (one by one)</h3>
              <p>Go through your friends, followers, and connections on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, TikTok — wherever you're already active.</p>
              <p><strong>Message 1:</strong></p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>Hey [First Name]!</p>
              </blockquote>
              <p><strong>Message 2</strong> (when they respond):</p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>I'm working on a new project — mind if I get your take on something?</p>
              </blockquote>
              <p><strong>Message 3</strong> (when they say sure):</p>
              <blockquote>
                <p>Cool, thanks! I'm starting a newsletter about [TOPIC] and thought of you because [personalized reason]. Mind if I add you to the list? Would love your thoughts.</p>
              </blockquote>

              <h3>2. Add sign-up links everywhere</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Social media bios (LinkedIn, Instagram, X, YouTube)</li>
                <li>Email signature</li>
                <li>Pinned posts</li>
                <li>Your website's sign-up form</li>
                <li>LinkedIn "Featured" section</li>
                <li>YouTube video descriptions and pinned comments</li>
              </ul>

              <h3>3. Announce it publicly</h3>
              <p>Tell people what you're doing, why, and how to join. One post. Doesn't need to be clever — just clear.</p>

              <h3>4. Mention it in your content</h3>
              <p>Bottom of every post: "Want more? Join my newsletter here 👉 [link]"</p>
              <p>End of every video or podcast: "I share more on this in my newsletter — link's in the description."</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- ── CASE STUDY: "TOO BORING" OBJECTION ─────────────────────── -->
      <div class="prose case-study">
        <h2>"My niche is too boring for this to work"</h2>
        <p>I hear this a lot. So here's a real one: a two-person finance team — regulated industry, about as "boring" as it gets — moved their LinkedIn audience over to an owned email list.</p>
        <p><strong>725 high-value subscribers. Zero algorithm reliance.</strong> 37% of those subscribers came straight from LinkedIn referrals.</p>
        <p>I helped them do it. We didn't do anything fancy — just the same plumbing you're setting up in this guide.</p>
        <p>That's it. That's the whole secret. If it works for a regulated finance team, it'll work for whatever you're doing.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── NEXT STEPS ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="prose next-steps">
        <h2>🚀 You're on your way</h2>
        <p>Right now, your only job is to get your first 50 subscribers. Don't overthink what comes next yet.</p>
        <p>Once you've got your 50, here's a sneak peek of what's next:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A welcome email sequence</li>
          <li>A proper sign-up / landing page</li>
          <li>Your first newsletter issue</li>
          <li>Repurposing your content into your newsletter</li>
          <li>Basic analytics so you know what's working</li>
          <li>...and more</li>
        </ul>
        <p>But for now — just focus on the 50.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── BONUS: MONETIZATION MENU ─────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="bonus-block">
        <p class="result-section-label">Bonus</p>
        <h2>The monetization menu — for once you've got a list</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>You don't need to figure this out today. But it helps to know what's possible once people start subscribing, so you're not starting from scratch later.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="mono-list">
          <div class="mono-item">
            <p class="mono-label">Service-Based Offers</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Done by You ($):</strong> Coaching, consulting, or small digital services you deliver yourself</li>
              <li><strong>Done with You ($$):</strong> Mentorship or group coaching</li>
              <li><strong>Done for You ($$$):</strong> Fully managed services</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mono-item">
            <p class="mono-label">Recurring Revenue</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Subscriptions:</strong> Premium content, exclusive reports, or a private community</li>
              <li><strong>Partnerships & Ads:</strong> Sponsors or ads in your newsletter</li>
              <li><strong>Affiliate Marketing:</strong> Recommend tools you actually use and earn a commission</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mono-item">
            <p class="mono-label">Education-Based Offers</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Courses:</strong> Online courses or workshops</li>
              <li><strong>Coaching:</strong> One-on-one or group sessions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mono-item">
            <p class="mono-label">Additional Revenue Streams</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Digital Products:</strong> Templates, checklists, ebooks</li>
              <li><strong>Beehiiv Boosts:</strong> Get paid to recommend other newsletters</li>
              <li><strong>Sponsored Content:</strong> Featured mentions in your newsletter</li>
              <li><strong>Physical Merchandise:</strong> Print-on-demand — t-shirts, mugs, and the like</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── FINAL CTA: DONE-FOR-YOU NEWSLETTER SETUP ──────────────────── -->
      <div class="cta-block final-cta">
        <div class="cta-card__label">Ready to skip the trial-and-error?</div>
        <h2>I'll just build it for you.</h2>
        <p>I had to figure all of this out myself — landing page, welcome emails, the survey that tells you who's actually on your list, syncing my content so I'm not manually re-posting everything. Took longer than I'd like to admit.</p>
        <p>If you'd rather skip the part where you learn it the hard way, I'll build the same setup I run, live in 72 hours. The Done-For-You Newsletter Setup is $497.</p>
        <a href="https://redefiningretirement.io/products/done-for-you-newsletter-set-up" class="btn">
          Get My Newsletter Set Up &rarr;
        </a>
        <p class="cta-note">Build guarantee: live within 72 hours, or I finish it free.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .narrow { max-width: 720px; }

    .article-header { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }

    .article-title {
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .article-deck {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      max-width: 640px;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    /* ── HELLO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .hello-section {
      display: flex;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      align-items: flex-start;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .hello-photo {
      width: 96px;
      height: 96px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      object-fit: cover;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      filter: grayscale(100%);
    }

    .hello-text h2 {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .hello-text p {
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    }

    .hello-text p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* ── READER QUOTE ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .reader-quote {
      margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--blue);
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    }

    .reader-quote p {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text);
      font-style: italic;
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    }

    .reader-quote p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .reader-quote-attr {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      font-style: normal !important;
    }

    /* ── VIDEO BLOCK ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .video-block {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .video-block-title {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .video-block-deck {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .video-block-note {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
      font-style: italic;
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .video-embed {
      position: relative;
      padding-bottom: 62.5%;
      height: 0;
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .video-embed iframe {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
    }

    /* ── NEXT STEPS ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .next-steps ul {
      margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }

    .next-steps li {
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
    }

    /* ── HOOK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .hook-block {
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .hook-block h2 {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .hook-block .prose p,
    .hook-block .prose ul {
      margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
    }

    .hook-block .prose p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    /* ── STEPS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .steps { margin: 2.5rem 0; }

    .step {
      display: flex;
      gap: 2rem;
      padding: 2.5rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .step:first-child { padding-top: 0; }
    .step:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

    .step-num {
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-weight: 900;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--blue);
      opacity: 0.5;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      width: 5rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
      padding-top: 0.3rem;
    }

    .step-content { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }

    .step-title {
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    /* ── INLINE CTA (Beehiiv affiliate) ───────────────────────────── */
    .inline-cta {
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--blue);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .inline-cta p {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .inline-cta p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      margin-top: 0.85rem;
    }

    .inline-cta .btn {
      display: flex;
      margin: 0 auto;
      width: fit-content;
    }

    .coupon {
      background: rgba(9, 161, 231, 0.1);
      color: var(--blue);
      padding: 0.15em 0.45em;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: monospace;
      font-size: 0.95em;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .cta-note {
      font-size: 0.76rem !important;
      color: var(--text-light) !important;
    }

    /* ── PROMPT BLOCK ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .prompt-block {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }

    .prompt-label {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .prompt-block pre {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 1rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    /* ── VIDEO PLACEHOLDER ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .video-placeholder {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      padding: 2rem;
      background: var(--bg-subtle);
      border: 1px dashed var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .video-placeholder p {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
      font-style: italic;
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ── BLOCKQUOTE (scripts) ──────────────────────────────────────── */
    .prose blockquote {
      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
